T|                                                            TIME CUT TO꞉            
N|               It's meal time. The uniformed Korean men sit down on the             
N|               ground and eat dinner. Their metal trays and cutlery clang           
N|               together noisily.                                                    
O|
N|               They shovel the food into their mouths, chatting about things        
N|               that young Korean men are concerned with, and complaining            
N|               about their utter exhaustion.                                        
O|
N|               All Korean men are required to serve in the military for two         
N|               years full‑time, be on reserve for six years, and attend a           
N|               few days of annual military training. One of these anonymous         
N|               men doing their compulsory national duty is Hae Sung, now 24         
N|               years old.                                                           
M|               It doesn't have to be clear to the audience that this is Hae         
M|               Sung. He just appears to be one of hundreds of ordinary              
M|               Korean men eating in the fields.                                     
O|
N|               Hae Sung looks up, remembering something.                            
